{
 "schema": 1,
 "name": "full_raids",
 "description": "M26 hard variant of `full`: the same village and standing orders, with random raids and zombie sieges ON (first siege after day 5, first raid after day 7) and the defences a player would plan (wall ring, one golem, two guards). M26-R target (orchestrator): the village survives the random raid with at least half its villagers, no strike lasts more than 2 days, and food is never out for more than a day running. Before M26-R the day-12 random raid on a Town of 16-19 killed 12-15 villagers in 2 of 2 runs (a Town was handed the full raid with 2-4 young guards) and the wage bill then outran the income for good. M26: a whole village over 30 days, starting at Hamlet, normal difficulty, random raids and zombie sieges on (the harness flag \"threats\": true; M25 rolls them with its grace days, so the first siege comes after day 5 and the first raid after day 7), weather fixed clear. Setup builds every building type on one 56 x 36 site (Village and Town buildings stay red until the tier) with a stone-age kit: 96 bread, planks, cobblestone, coal, stone tools, a bow, 32 emeralds, 12 adults. The scenario then plays a pretend player: day 1 it hires a farmer x2, a lumberjack and a cook; the standing orders (each runs once, when the tier allows it, and the hire is kept filled afterwards) hire a merchant, miner, hunter, two guards and a builder at Village and a blacksmith at Town. No other input. The roadmap criteria are the assertions: reaches Village, food days left is never 0 two dawns running, the treasury is never negative (VillageState rejects a negative purse, so this one cannot fail at L3: it is proven at L1 by PayRunTest), village logic under 1 ms a tick. Targets (tier_town, strikes, births) are reported in the summary, not asserted. The 12 adults are topped up at day 1 tick 400, after the first ticks, when one of the vanilla villagers is lost to the harness's ground re-grading (in_wall at tick ~190 on seed 1, a harness effect, not game logic). Defences, chosen at the start like a player's plan: a 56 x 36 cobblestone wall ring with two gates (700 cobblestone and 10 fence gates in the Storage kit, built the moment Village unlocks walls, by the harness's instant `build` as a standing order, one iron golem, and the two guards of `full` (the Barracks has four beds; a third and fourth guard would raise the wage bill by 4 emeralds a day and the income does not follow: the first M26-R run with four guards drained the treasury by day 21).",
 "default_days": 30,
